# =============================================================================
# Frontend environment — apps/web
#
# Copy to `.env.local`. There is deliberately almost nothing here.
# =============================================================================

# Where Next.js proxies /api/v1 to. Read in next.config.ts at build and server
# start, NOT in the browser: it has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on purpose.
#
# The browser only ever calls /api/v1 on its own origin, and Next rewrites that
# to FastAPI. That indirection is what lets the refresh cookie stay
# SameSite=Lax — a cross-origin API would force SameSite=None, and a cookie
# that travels on third-party requests is the thing SameSite exists to stop.
#
# Under docker compose this becomes the service name: http://api:8000
API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# Optional. Node's own setting, not ours; listed because `next dev -p` and this
# disagreeing is a common five-minute confusion.
# PORT=3000
